✅ 3.What if we call run() directly?

Example: thread.run();

Output:
🔴 main thread started
🔴 main thread ended

Why ?
🔴 run() is just a normal Java method.
🔴 Calling run() does not create a new thread.
🔴 The run() method executes the same thread that invoked it (usually the main thread).
🔴 The Thread Scheduler is not involved because no new thread is created.
🔴 Execution is synchronous, not concurrent.



Internal Flow

Main Thread
     │ calls run()
     ▼
run() executes
     │
     ▼
Main Thread continues execution